WEBVTT

00:02.080 --> 00:05.440
Good grief. You drove a costly bargain.

00:06.160 --> 00:12.280
A 200-year contract conditional on 
buying back your corpse from the guild?

00:12.280 --> 00:14.180
Dragons do think differently.

00:14.540 --> 00:17.410
Your pardon, master of my temporary lodging.

00:18.170 --> 00:23.750
I could not stomach virtual strangers 
having their way with my flesh.

00:24.430 --> 00:30.930
I much prefer an apprentice of my slayer,
 the "Wandering Balcony."

00:30.930 --> 00:32.670
Don't mind him, my foolish pupil.

00:33.210 --> 00:36.180
Just remember that it takes all kinds.

00:36.180 --> 00:41.260
Once again, my mortal remains are yours

00:41.260 --> 00:48.190
to fashion into weapons, reanimate 
as a pawn, compound into medicine,

00:48.780 --> 00:51.980
or use to forge new ties.

00:53.770 --> 00:57.050
I just linked you to a dragon.

02:31.750 --> 02:35.250
Novels with adventurers' 
guilds and shark movies

02:35.250 --> 02:37.370
are a lot alike, if you ask me.

02:37.790 --> 02:41.390
Are you <i>trying</i> to throw 
fans of both for a loop?

02:41.850 --> 02:46.930
The familiar adventurers' guild 
is a prop in isekai fantasy.

02:46.930 --> 02:53.230
<b>Guild</b>

02:47.210 --> 02:53.230
Then each novel adds its own original 
spin to tell different stories, right?

02:53.470 --> 02:55.560
Shark movies are the same way.

02:55.560 --> 02:58.320
They share the same prop, a man-eating shark,

02:58.320 --> 03:01.210
but they make it a tornado, or a ghost, 
or a demon, or a zombie,

03:01.210 --> 03:04.200
or swim in sand or snow, 
or atomic, or robotic, or mecha,

03:04.200 --> 03:09.480
or have two or three or—
fast forward—six heads.

03:09.480 --> 03:11.040
That's how they add originality, you know?

03:11.260 --> 03:14.480
I mean, doesn't that go for 
samurai movies or westerns, too?

03:14.480 --> 03:15.130
True.

03:15.130 --> 03:19.380
Meaning you could argue samurai movies 
and westerns are shark movies, too.

03:19.640 --> 03:24.850
And they say Shakespeare wrote the 
blueprint for every story there is,

03:25.070 --> 03:29.310
<b>Sharkspeare</b>

03:25.870 --> 03:29.310
so maybe Shakespeare was a shark?

03:25.870 --> 03:29.310
<b>Author of "Shark for Shark"</b>

03:29.860 --> 03:32.020
Please just get to the point already.

03:32.360 --> 03:37.220
I'm trying to say we should check how 
original Misaki-chan is as a vampire.

03:37.220 --> 03:38.880
Huh? Me?

03:38.880 --> 03:40.990
Talk about taking the long way round.

03:41.300 --> 03:45.960
How is Misaki-chan different 
from your standard "vampire" prop?

03:45.960 --> 03:48.160
I think that's worth knowing.

03:48.500 --> 03:52.710
We don't want enemies learning her 
strengths and weaknesses, either.

03:53.370 --> 03:55.360
Well, you've got me there.

03:55.850 --> 03:57.630
Are you okay in sunlight?

03:57.630 --> 04:01.160
Yup! It kind of dazzles me, but that's all.

04:01.160 --> 04:03.530
Okay, then. Do you suck blood?

04:03.530 --> 04:04.260
Huh?

04:04.260 --> 04:09.270
The Corpse God told me that 
blood is like steroids for her.

04:09.600 --> 04:11.190
And to make more vampires,

04:11.190 --> 04:16.480
she'd need to give a lot of blood over a long 
time, so she won't do it by accident.

04:16.480 --> 04:22.010
But with access to magic, upgrades—
I mean, "evolution"—could be easy.

04:22.930 --> 04:27.050
The Corpse God turning Misaki-chan 
into a vampire is a good example.

04:27.050 --> 04:29.630
It's like I got superpowers!

04:31.310 --> 04:32.870
<b>He's like a 
superhero!</b>

04:34.560 --> 04:35.390
Sorry.

04:36.510 --> 04:38.870
I got you mixed up in my problems.

04:39.630 --> 04:43.550
That arm is the greatest 
show of faith I can offer.

04:43.860 --> 04:49.300
I swear by the dragon it belonged to 
and my teacher, who gave it to me:

04:49.640 --> 04:51.590
I trust you.

04:52.250 --> 04:56.650
So, would you become my ally 
and lend me your strength?

05:00.310 --> 05:04.900
It's hard to believe, but after 
seeing those tigers and now this...

05:05.660 --> 05:07.840
By the way, what's that plush shark?

05:07.840 --> 05:10.160
Oh, this is the real Polka-kun.

05:10.370 --> 05:11.080
Huh?

05:11.080 --> 05:15.820
<i>He means that Polka's 
possessing that toy shark.</i>

05:15.140 --> 05:16.620
<b>A robot arm
and a dragon arm</b>

05:15.820 --> 05:17.070
Umm...

05:17.070 --> 05:22.330
<i>He seems to enjoy it so much 
that I couldn't stay mad.</i>

05:22.330 --> 05:23.840
I... see.

05:24.270 --> 05:30.630
<i>He even gave me some nonsense about wanting 
a robot body instead of his old one.</i>

05:32.410 --> 05:35.410
<b>It's great to
 have you
 on board</b>

05:32.660 --> 05:36.090
He, er, says to give his 
best to you, Xiaoyu-kun.

05:36.620 --> 05:37.390
Likewise.

05:37.390 --> 05:42.320
<b>EEK 
EEK
 EEK</b>

05:37.870 --> 05:42.320
Master Polka, it's <i>so nice</i> to see you again.

05:38.580 --> 05:42.320
<b>A robot hand!
A dragon hand!</b>

05:42.600 --> 05:46.320
<i>Wait, does he sound </i>more <i>
hostile than he did to me?</i>

05:46.700 --> 05:50.330
W-Well, anyway, I'd appreciate your help.

05:50.980 --> 05:53.770
We know that someone is out to get us.

05:54.270 --> 05:57.340
And as for the group using 
the imperial emblem,

05:57.790 --> 06:00.330
I'd like to take any steps I can.

06:02.340 --> 06:07.470
You'll do better at smoking 
them out, summer bug.

06:05.460 --> 06:09.390
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

06:07.470 --> 06:10.290
You'll benefit, too.

06:10.290 --> 06:15.100
Summer bug in search of 
something beyond reason.

06:15.100 --> 06:16.560
Oh?

06:16.790 --> 06:22.250
Their founder was a bastard child 
from the other side of the sky.

06:22.250 --> 06:25.030
A bug eating away at this world.

06:25.030 --> 06:27.190
The other side of the sky?

06:27.560 --> 06:29.610
Do you mean a space alien?!

06:29.950 --> 06:32.200
We don't know the specifics,

06:32.650 --> 06:37.710
but they are one of those 
close to what you seek.

06:38.080 --> 06:41.610
<i>One</i> of those? Meaning you have more leads?

06:41.610 --> 06:46.440
You should know them well, too, summer bug.

06:47.480 --> 06:49.050
I suppose so.

06:49.300 --> 06:54.300
If my blimp show set all of this in motion,

06:54.510 --> 06:59.020
then it must all connect somewhere.

06:59.250 --> 07:02.060
Including to you, of course,

07:02.380 --> 07:04.570
Fire-Breathing Bug-kun.

07:07.370 --> 07:08.570
You're back.

07:08.570 --> 07:12.780
Yup, although I'll be splitting my 
time between here and HQ for a bit.

07:13.340 --> 07:14.950
That's an awfully old file.

07:15.340 --> 07:17.930
I'm going over the Fire-Breathing Bug's past,

07:17.930 --> 07:21.290
since we know they're at odds 
with Habaki's group now.

07:21.290 --> 07:22.750
Huh.

07:22.750 --> 07:25.250
Would it kill you to act surprised for once?

07:25.650 --> 07:28.310
The Bug first appeared a few years ago,

07:28.310 --> 07:31.190
or so the police and the media thought.

07:31.190 --> 07:32.340
It's true, isn't it?

07:32.340 --> 07:38.390
<b>Classified</b>

07:32.340 --> 07:38.390
<b>This world is
 a buggy program

so it cries out 
for the flame</b>

07:32.810 --> 07:34.550
This morning, I discovered

07:34.550 --> 07:38.390
that they only started 
using English recently.

07:39.810 --> 07:43.190
Meaning that the Fire-Breathing 
Bug was around long before

07:43.410 --> 07:45.630
I joined Comps-3.

07:43.790 --> 07:46.150
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

07:47.170 --> 07:48.110
Okay!

07:48.400 --> 07:51.030
Would the next person please come this way?

07:51.030 --> 07:53.520
This place seems quite popular.

07:53.520 --> 07:55.510
Who knew it'd be this packed?

07:56.020 --> 07:58.140
What is it, Soara-san?

07:58.140 --> 08:01.790
Well, I'm not sure, but my skin...

08:02.050 --> 08:04.750
No, my blood is tingling.

08:04.750 --> 08:05.840
Well, now.

08:05.840 --> 08:08.730
Somethin' about this place weirds me out.

08:07.840 --> 08:10.010
I'm jealous!

08:10.340 --> 08:15.890
You must have sensed something! 
Some power not of this world!

08:16.130 --> 08:19.350
After all, this fortune teller 
is as real as they come!

08:19.350 --> 08:21.070
<i>What the heck are <i>those</i>?!</i>

08:19.620 --> 08:22.830
Look, this video is of this very building!

08:20.180 --> 08:23.440
<b>crows to talk!</b>

08:21.080 --> 08:23.930
<i>Hands! They're hands!</i>

08:22.830 --> 08:26.440
Yes, I heard the Phantom 
Solitaire was involved.

08:26.440 --> 08:30.530
Public opinion may lean that way, 
but I see things differently.

08:31.660 --> 08:35.360
Solitaire is always winging it,
 looking for thrills,

08:35.360 --> 08:38.580
but he loves to astonish his audience.

08:39.040 --> 08:44.540
It wouldn't make sense for him to put 
on such a big display with no warning.

08:44.850 --> 08:49.640
If it wasn't a trick, did something 
genuinely supernatural attack Solitaire?

08:49.640 --> 08:51.990
No, not necessarily.

08:51.990 --> 08:53.010
How so?

08:53.010 --> 08:57.720
Maybe he was doing a merry 
dance with those weird hands.

09:01.230 --> 09:04.270
What a positively delightful idea!

09:04.580 --> 09:07.480
I know, right? In the 
real spirit of adventure!

09:10.460 --> 09:13.260
Number 25, please come this way!

09:13.260 --> 09:15.280
Oh, I think we're up.

09:16.010 --> 09:17.410
May I ask your name?

09:18.070 --> 09:19.890
I'm Mikoto.

09:20.350 --> 09:22.240
Mikoto Saimyouji.

09:22.240 --> 09:26.540
Search it in the Latin alphabet 
to find my socials. Look me up!

09:26.540 --> 09:28.000
<b>FORTUNES TOLD </b>

09:26.540 --> 09:28.000
<b>Reception desk opens at 10:00 a.m. 
Please fill out the questionnaire 
you receive with your name, 
date of birth, etc. 
We use personal information
 for fortune-telling only 
and destroy records after use.</b>

09:28.440 --> 09:31.360
You really hit it off with that guy.

09:31.360 --> 09:33.960
Yes, I think we'll get along swimmingly.

09:34.750 --> 09:35.690
Well now.

09:35.690 --> 09:36.930
What is it?

09:37.480 --> 09:40.240
It says he's a medical examiner.

09:40.240 --> 09:40.970
I see.

09:41.270 --> 09:45.020
Next. Your name and what you'd 
like a fortune about, please.

09:45.020 --> 09:48.050
Sure. Put my name down as "Civil."

09:45.020 --> 09:50.500
<b><b>Let's get
examining!</b></b>

09:45.020 --> 09:50.500
<b>Edit</b>

09:45.020 --> 09:50.500
<b>I practice forensic medicine in Tokyo! 
Let's get examining!</b>

09:48.050 --> 09:49.830
As for what I'd like divined...

09:50.740 --> 09:55.030
My fate over 100 years, 
and also fresh encounters.

09:56.300 --> 09:59.280
I'd like Dr. Saimyouji's opinion.

09:59.620 --> 10:00.910
Is he in today?

10:01.160 --> 10:02.900
I haven't seen him.

10:02.900 --> 10:05.050
He must be as busy as we are.

10:05.050 --> 10:07.790
How does he always find time 
to drop in on us, then?

10:08.020 --> 10:12.500
I hear he's hooked on a spiritualist lately.
 Hilarious.

10:12.500 --> 10:13.330
Huh?

10:13.330 --> 10:17.130
A boy fortune teller who 
suddenly popped up in Shinjuku.

10:17.130 --> 10:20.090
Really? A boy who tells fortu—

10:20.090 --> 10:20.990
Wait!

10:21.550 --> 10:23.510
<b>On Break</b>

10:23.510 --> 10:27.730
That mechanical pencil... 
is Inspector Hosorogi?

10:27.730 --> 10:30.190
Heh heh heh. Pleased to meet you, young man.

10:30.430 --> 10:35.190
Huh. I bet the Phantom Solitaire 
would be shocked to find that out.

10:35.190 --> 10:39.030
Huh? Oh, when I fought him...

10:39.030 --> 10:42.490
<b>Solitaire lying his head off</b>

10:39.030 --> 10:42.490
I'll repay Hosorogi some other time!

10:42.750 --> 10:45.000
He seemed awfully concerned,

10:45.000 --> 10:49.710
so I figured Inspector Hosorogi 
must have done a lot for Solitaire.

10:50.000 --> 10:51.460
Have you really?

10:52.270 --> 10:53.020
No! Absolutely not! First I've heard of it!

10:53.020 --> 10:56.000
No! Absolutely not! First I've heard of it! 
This is getting scary! Help!

10:53.560 --> 10:56.000
<b>A Mis<i>lead</i> Pencil</b>

10:56.410 --> 11:00.770
The Phantom Solitaire... 
I wonder what he's after?

11:01.120 --> 11:02.970
Do you mind if I call the next person?

11:02.970 --> 11:03.600
Oh.

11:03.840 --> 11:05.400
Yes, please do.

11:05.400 --> 11:07.810
I'll get back to work, too, then.

11:08.230 --> 11:11.770
Sayo-sama requested 
kiritanpo stew for dinner.

11:12.480 --> 11:14.110
That sounds nice.

11:17.070 --> 11:18.070
<i>What?</i>

11:18.700 --> 11:21.660
<i>What's approaching?</i>

11:22.010 --> 11:23.580
Your next client.

11:27.930 --> 11:29.640
Pardon the intrusion.

11:33.210 --> 11:36.130
Hello, I'm called Civil.

11:46.420 --> 11:47.560
Pleased to meet you.

11:50.660 --> 11:52.230
<i>I can't believe it.</i>

11:53.080 --> 11:58.230
<i>I've never seen so many ghosts 
cluster to a single person.</i>

11:58.780 --> 12:04.310
<i>Even killing a million people in a war 
wouldn't explain all this.</i>

12:04.720 --> 12:09.970
<i>These shades have been maturing 
for years or even decades.</i>

12:10.470 --> 12:11.640
<i>And...</i>

12:11.640 --> 12:14.150
<i>very few of them harbor malice.</i>

12:14.150 --> 12:16.710
<i>Most linger not out of regret or love,</i>

12:16.710 --> 12:18.040
<i>but obsession.</i>

12:18.520 --> 12:19.990
Is something wrong?

12:19.990 --> 12:22.130
<i>I can't let him see me panic.</i>

12:22.380 --> 12:25.430
<i>I'll cast a false-face spell on myself</i>

12:25.720 --> 12:27.890
<i>to appear composed.</i>

12:29.830 --> 12:34.400
I see that you've led a most... 
peculiar life.

12:34.400 --> 12:39.360
Oh, yes? Everyone says that, 
but it's duller than you'd think.

12:39.360 --> 12:40.720
<i>Hey, what's up?</i>

12:39.360 --> 12:41.070
<b>SHIVER
SHIVER
SHIVER</b>

12:39.600 --> 12:43.530
Doubtless because you've 
grown numb to your condition.

12:41.070 --> 12:43.530
You're doing a normal reading, right?

12:44.540 --> 12:47.540
<i>I can't tell if he's a fraud or not,</i>

12:48.340 --> 12:52.580
<i>but judging by the gear the people 
watching this building carried,</i>

12:52.580 --> 12:56.470
<i>their mission was to observe 
and protect this fortune teller.</i>

12:57.280 --> 12:59.420
<i>I'd better probe deeper.</i>

13:00.330 --> 13:01.890
By the way,

13:01.890 --> 13:05.590
I hear a famous criminal called 
Solitaire visited this building.

13:05.590 --> 13:07.210
So it seems.

13:07.210 --> 13:08.610
You haven't met him?

13:08.970 --> 13:09.790
No.

13:09.790 --> 13:14.770
Although our fates may already have 
intersected without my realizing it.

13:15.370 --> 13:17.230
Hmm...

13:17.230 --> 13:20.630
I suspected this computer 
wouldn't be up to the task.

13:20.630 --> 13:23.780
Good thing I asked Nanny 
to handle production.

13:25.160 --> 13:27.240
What are you doing?

13:28.150 --> 13:29.300
Yesterday, you—

13:29.300 --> 13:32.870
I'm hungry, so I'm leaving. So long.

13:33.080 --> 13:37.440
I can't believe you'd take 
off and leave me in this fix.

13:37.440 --> 13:39.920
Oh, just a wicked scheme of mine.

13:39.920 --> 13:44.920
Forget that and work on smiling 
more pleasantly, like an idol.

13:45.330 --> 13:47.050
Please be reasonable.

13:47.050 --> 13:51.040
Don't fret. I have every faith in you!

13:51.040 --> 13:53.860
Forget that. Where's my phone?

13:53.860 --> 13:56.020
The cops might trace the signal.

13:56.290 --> 13:59.100
Already incinerated.

13:59.100 --> 14:01.310
It wasn't cheap, you know?

14:01.310 --> 14:06.010
You fear the police more than me?

14:06.010 --> 14:07.530
It depends.

14:07.810 --> 14:11.490
You mean the Bastard Children of Sabaramond?

14:11.490 --> 14:14.730
Sabaramond? What's that?

14:15.040 --> 14:17.960
I just remembered a detective named Arase.

14:18.200 --> 14:21.100
What he might do scares me more than dying.

14:22.650 --> 14:24.770
You really don't know, then?

14:24.770 --> 14:27.510
Nope. I haven't got a clue.

14:28.700 --> 14:31.660
Then, we're in this together!

14:31.660 --> 14:32.100
What?

14:34.060 --> 14:37.520
<b>I have completed your request. Kindly confirm.</b>

14:34.060 --> 14:37.520
<b>To me</b>

14:34.060 --> 14:37.520
<b>Nanny</b>

14:34.060 --> 14:37.520
<b><i><u>Phantom Solitaire's Grand Operation: Thrilling Surprise.zip</u></i></b>

14:34.060 --> 14:37.520
<b>I have completed your request, Young Master. Kindly confirm. 

I would appreciate it if you would deposit your fee into the usual account. 


You mustn't let yourself go hungry or catch a chill, now.</b>

14:37.960 --> 14:42.590
Let's ferret out the secret 
of this "Sabaramond."

14:42.590 --> 14:45.190
The two of us, together.

14:47.080 --> 14:48.150
Now,

14:48.420 --> 14:51.340
you asked about your "fate over 100 years."

14:51.340 --> 14:54.630
Would you care to elaborate?

14:54.630 --> 14:57.270
Well, for example,

14:57.270 --> 15:00.310
suppose someone committed 
an unforgivable crime.

15:00.620 --> 15:03.770
Do you think that not only the 
criminal but those close to them

15:03.770 --> 15:07.550
should face the world's curses and judgment?

15:10.530 --> 15:13.600
This is merely my personal opinion,

15:14.010 --> 15:17.350
but I hope that this world 
wouldn't do such a thing.

15:17.350 --> 15:20.440
Do you? Well, I suppose most people would.

15:21.180 --> 15:23.300
But my fellows and I

15:24.340 --> 15:29.990
are hounded by a dangerous bunch 
over a 100-year-old grudge.

15:32.560 --> 15:34.750
That must be trying.

15:34.750 --> 15:39.910
Please allow me to assist 
you in any way I can.

15:40.290 --> 15:42.370
<i>Trying</i>?

15:43.190 --> 15:44.790
Au contraire, my good fortune teller.

15:45.980 --> 15:50.510
I want to meet those masses of 
irrationality as soon as possible.

15:50.770 --> 15:51.430
What?

15:51.840 --> 15:53.390
Just think about it.

15:53.900 --> 16:01.850
When someone hits, resents, despises, 
or even wants to kill you,

16:02.090 --> 16:05.310
the more absurd their reasons, the better.

16:06.350 --> 16:08.020
What do you mean?

16:08.660 --> 16:10.910
We've done nothing wrong,

16:10.910 --> 16:14.990
so we can crush the bugs 
with a clear conscience

16:15.480 --> 16:17.950
and without remorse.

16:19.940 --> 16:21.160
Doesn't that

16:21.940 --> 16:25.070
amount to doing the same thing they are?

16:25.380 --> 16:28.840
Yes, so it comes down to the order.

16:29.290 --> 16:31.930
Someone in my camp committed a crime.

16:30.570 --> 16:36.030
<b>Crime</b>

16:32.250 --> 16:36.280
Revenge against that criminal is justifiable.

16:32.440 --> 16:36.030
<b>Revenge</b>

16:36.030 --> 16:46.230
<b>Crime</b>

16:36.030 --> 16:46.230
<b>Revenge</b>

16:36.280 --> 16:43.840
But if the avengers hate me and 
mine just for having ties to them,

16:43.840 --> 16:46.230
that constitutes a new attack.

16:46.230 --> 16:51.940
So aren't we justified even if we 
target the people close to <i>them</i>?

16:52.510 --> 16:54.900
<i>He's... different!</i>

16:54.900 --> 17:01.240
As long as we evade the eyes of the law, 
we can inflict any violence or indignity.

17:01.240 --> 17:04.870
Don't you think that's delightful?

17:05.350 --> 17:09.090
<i>He isn't like those children.</i>

17:09.610 --> 17:16.590
<i>Those innocent children who were 
murdered just for being with me.</i>

17:17.230 --> 17:19.560
Let me ask you one question.

17:19.560 --> 17:23.810
Do you truly believe every 
word you've just said?

17:24.250 --> 17:25.680
I wonder.

17:25.680 --> 17:27.770
Why don't you divine the answer?

17:29.130 --> 17:31.690
Yes, I'll do just that.

17:46.700 --> 17:48.330
What's up, Lulu?

17:49.110 --> 17:51.290
Huh? I suddenly don't feel so...

17:51.290 --> 17:52.750
Huh? What?

17:52.750 --> 17:55.050
I... I'm sorry. I'd like to cancel today.

17:53.650 --> 17:55.050
I'd better go.

17:55.050 --> 17:55.640
Huh?

17:55.640 --> 17:56.720
Huh?

18:00.200 --> 18:01.090
<i>I thought so.</i>

18:01.090 --> 18:03.430
<i>He hasn't noticed what I'm doing.</i>

18:03.870 --> 18:09.100
<i>So at least he doesn't have the 
Evil Eye to see ghosts and spirits.</i>

18:09.470 --> 18:10.960
<i>Going forward,</i>

18:14.200 --> 18:18.380
<i>I'll touch his soul directly and rattle him.</i>

18:19.300 --> 18:22.570
Please allow yourself 
to move with this space.

18:22.880 --> 18:24.830
Calm your mind.

18:30.090 --> 18:31.750
<i>Are these shades</i>

18:32.410 --> 18:34.380
<i>trying to shield him?</i>

18:44.370 --> 18:46.650
<i>I've never felt anything like this.</i>

18:47.230 --> 18:49.850
<i>A burst of mana inside my body.</i>

18:50.570 --> 18:52.140
<i>What just happened to me?</i>

18:52.660 --> 18:53.820
<i>Don't tell me</i>

18:53.820 --> 18:57.940
<i>this boy is a visitor from another world?</i>

18:59.110 --> 19:02.040
<i>How is his mana so dense?!</i>

19:02.390 --> 19:04.950
<i>It's on par with an imperial court sorcerer!</i>

19:05.640 --> 19:09.290
<i>Is he really a human from this world?!</i>

19:10.050 --> 19:16.050
<i>But I've already verified that Polka 
Shinoyama is a native of this world.</i>

19:16.310 --> 19:19.930
<i>Is he a double? Is he something 
from beyond the sky?</i>

19:20.280 --> 19:23.760
<i>Or is someone controlling him?</i>

19:24.240 --> 19:25.720
<i>Fascinating.</i>

19:26.150 --> 19:28.330
What a strange sensation.

19:28.330 --> 19:31.660
Did you just do something to me, 
by any chance?

19:32.270 --> 19:38.570
Who can say? You may have felt a 
dormant fate awaken within you.

19:39.560 --> 19:43.660
Please allow me to probe your 
soul a little more deeply.

19:44.320 --> 19:49.120
<i>Avoiding conflict now would be smarter, 
but I want just a little more.</i>

19:49.120 --> 19:52.580
Oh? I can't wait to see what comes out.

19:53.110 --> 19:58.550
I'd love to know what's 
hiding inside me, too.

19:59.130 --> 20:02.010
You may be happier not knowing

20:02.530 --> 20:04.970
the "real" you.

20:04.970 --> 20:06.140
Civil-sama!

20:07.000 --> 20:08.610
I received guidance!

20:08.610 --> 20:10.310
We're not safe here!

20:10.570 --> 20:12.270
<i>Who is this girl?</i>

20:13.030 --> 20:15.480
<i>That's a high-ranking stone elemental.</i>

20:16.580 --> 20:21.400
Is this the child? The one 
who was sold off young?

20:17.040 --> 20:21.400
<b>Byadian Imperial Chancellor 

Leuf Vellize</b>

20:17.040 --> 20:21.400
m 0 0 l 260 0 260 70 0 70

20:21.790 --> 20:25.950
His people should always have 
been able to see spirits,

20:25.950 --> 20:28.620
but Evil Eyes were still too much for them.

20:29.210 --> 20:34.570
You can only <i>hear</i> the spirits, 
can't you, my lady chancellor?

20:35.550 --> 20:38.630
The Evil Eye is hearing as much as sight.

20:39.510 --> 20:42.980
You must suffer worse than 
we who can do only one.

20:44.830 --> 20:47.070
But live strong.

20:47.520 --> 20:53.630
Shades and elementals are our 
neighbors, always by our sides.

20:55.350 --> 20:56.650
<i>I see.</i>

20:56.650 --> 20:59.770
Can't you do something? 
It was just getting good.

20:59.770 --> 21:01.640
But the guidance...

21:01.640 --> 21:04.950
Give it up, Boss! You can't 
argue with Lulu's ears.

21:05.640 --> 21:08.170
<i>And the color of that woman's soul, too...</i>

21:08.170 --> 21:12.410
Plus, the Bugs might come torch this place.

21:12.640 --> 21:16.060
<i>"Bugs"? Are they involved 
with the Fire-Breathing Bug?</i>

21:16.060 --> 21:17.130
<i>No, more importantly,</i>

21:17.700 --> 21:20.470
<i>one could have been coincidence,</i>

21:20.470 --> 21:24.870
<i>but here are three people 
deeply mixed up in my world.</i>

21:25.430 --> 21:27.140
<i>This must be fate.</i>

21:27.790 --> 21:30.380
<i>These children came to see me</i>

21:30.380 --> 21:32.810
<i>as previous visitors to this world!</i>

21:33.490 --> 21:38.000
<i>I used ghosts to chase off 
my clients, but what now?</i>

21:38.000 --> 21:39.030
<i>Should I have them stay?</i>

21:39.030 --> 21:41.270
Come on! Move it!

21:41.920 --> 21:43.740
Sorry, my good fortune teller.

21:43.740 --> 21:45.800
I'll pay you another visit.

21:45.800 --> 21:48.320
Next time, as a friend.

21:52.580 --> 21:54.330
Soara-san!

21:59.430 --> 22:04.170
You must be the attacker who's 
been scurrying around lately.
